==Match==

===Summary===
[[File:FCP-CL Supporters.jpg|thumb|203x203px|FC Porto supporters at the Gelsenkirchen Arena AufSchalke.]]
Monaco, in their first European final since the 1992 Europa Cup,<ref name=bbcsport /> were up against Porto, the UEFA Cup winners from the previous season,<ref name=bbcsport /> who were appearing in the European Cup final for a second time, after defeating [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]] in the [[1987 European Cup final]].<ref name=uefareport>{{cite web |url=http://www.uefa.com/competitions/UCL/FixturesResults/Round=1716/Match=1065206/Report=RP.html |title=Porto perform to perfection |publisher=UEFA |date=26 May 2004 |first= Adam |last=Szreter  |access-date=22 September 2019 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20040603134348/http://www.uefa.com/competitions/UCL/FixturesResults/Round=1716/Match=1065206/Report=RP.html | archive-date=3 June 2004| url-status=dead }}</ref> Porto were the favourites after eliminating Manchester United and Deportivo La Coruña in the knockout phase, while Monaco had eliminated Real Madrid and Chelsea.{{Citation needed|date=May 2023}} Porto won the match 3–0; [[Carlos Alberto (footballer, born December 1984)|Carlos Alberto]] opened the scoring in the first half, while [[Deco]] and [[Dmitri Alenichev]] extended Porto's lead in the second half.<ref>{{cite news |last1=McCarra |first1=Kevin |title=Mourinho leaves Porto on top |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2004/may/27/match.porto |access-date=14 March 2024 |work=The Guardian |date=26 May 2004}}</ref>

